post.description:
Starts the device's live preview and holds the device for you (`session_id` becomes `manual_<yourUserId>_<udid>`), so automation is not given it while you watch. iOS starts WebDriverAgent's MJPEG stream (and the go-ios tunnel on iOS 17+). Android starts an MJPEG screen capture, or, when the server's `streaming.androidH264` setting is on and the device is not being recorded, an H.264 stream for the WebSocket in `h264Path`. Missing screen dimensions are filled in and saved.
Who may start:
- a free device: anyone who can see it;
- a device you already hold, or running your own Appium session: you (the preview runs alongside it);
- a device held by someone whose preview is no longer running (left over from a restart): anyone; the old hold is cleared;
- otherwise `409`, naming the holder. Admins may always start.
Needs the `MEMBER` role and the `devices` scope.
On a hub, for a node's phone, the request is forwarded to the node, which holds the phone by its own rules; on success the hub also marks the phone busy and held by you at once. A cloud provider's phone answers `501`.
One capture per Android device where it can be. A page that shows MJPEG (a browser that cannot decode H.264, which on plain http it cannot, or a page whose H.264 player failed) sends `player: mjpeg`: the server then starts the MJPEG capture, and ends an H.264 capture running for the device once nobody plays it: first, if nobody does, else when its last viewer leaves. Another page may still be playing it, and keeps it until then. A node on 2.13 or older ignores `player`.

get.description:
The caller's API tokens that haven't been revoked, newest first, including expired ones. The
token values themselves are never returned after creation. Any signed-in user may call it;
with authentication disabled it lists the first `SUPER_ADMIN`'s tokens.

A self-contained zip of the recording, for the phones the caller can see:

- `manifest.json`: the group and each phone's recording (id, status, times, size);
- `README.md`: a readable summary;
- `composite.mp4`, when there is a composite the caller may have (marks burned in when
  that rendering works);
- per phone, under `devices/<udid>/`: `video.mp4` (as recorded, no marks),
  `bookmarks.json`, `annotations.json` and `device.json`.

Streamed as it is built: an error after it has started cuts the download short. Any
signed-in user may call it.
